committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790602650 +0900

Add cited-cluster binding granularity; merge runs in E1 analysis

Read-set cluster keys include high-churn clusters (newsletter threads), so
false invalidation barely drops below source-epoch keys (0.93 vs 1.00 on
the first dev world-branch). The cited granularity binds the clusters of
the writer's own citations -- the item's support set -- taken from the
shared writer output in both D arms so that D cannot leak into detection
(tested). E1 cells and baselines are configurable; the analysis merges
several runs and writes to an explicit output directory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
